.TH PDFLUENT-PAGES 1  "pdfluent 1.1.0" PDFluent
.SH NAME
pdfluent\-pages \- Rotate, delete, reorder, or extract pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpdfluent pages\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-rotate\fR] [\fB\-\-delete\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-reorder\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-extract\fR] [\fB\-\-pages\fR] <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR> [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rotate, delete, reorder, or extract pages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON envelope on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-rotate\fR \fI<DEG>\fR
Rotate pages by degrees: 90, 180, 270 (negatives allowed). Applies to `\-\-pages`, or every page without it
.TP
\fB\-\-delete\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Delete pages, e.g. `2,5\-7`
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet: human mode prints data only (no warnings or progress notes)
.TP
\fB\-\-reorder\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
New page order, e.g. `3,1,2`: every page exactly once
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose stderr diagnostics (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-\-extract\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Keep only these pages, e.g. `1\-3,5`
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Pages `\-\-rotate` applies to. Default: every page
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output PDF, or `\-` for stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite the existing output file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Input PDF, or `\-` for stdin
.SH VERSION
v1.1.0
